/** @page mysqlnativebulkloadguide Native LOAD DATA Bulk Loading

    @tableofcontents

    When built against a %Qore library with the native bulk-load DBI API and a compatible MySQL or
    MariaDB client library, this driver implements \c DBI_CAP_HAS_BULK_LOAD with callback-driven
    \c LOAD \c DATA \c LOCAL \c INFILE.  No file is created or read: each BulkSqlUtil block is
    serialized in memory and supplied synchronously through \c mysql_set_local_infile_handler().
    The native path is insert-only and remains explicitly opt-in.

    @code{.py}
%requires BulkSqlUtil
%requires SqlUtil

Datasource ds("mysql:user/password@db%host:3306");
SqlUtil::AbstractTable table = (new SqlUtil::Table(ds, "event_log")).getTable();
BulkSqlUtil::BulkInsertOperation op(table, {
    "bulk_load": True,       # require native loading; "auto" permits fallback
    "block_size": 1000,
});
on_error {
    op.discard();
    ds.rollback();
}
map op.queueData($1), events.iterator();
op.flush();
op.endStream();
ds.commit();
    @endcode

    Native loading is dynamically available only when the server's global \c local_infile setting is
    enabled and the target table uses the transactional \c InnoDB or \c XtraDB engine. Table and
    column names must be simple, unquoted MySQL identifiers; a table may be qualified once by its
    schema. \c "bulk_load": \c "auto" uses the ordinary insert path when these conditions are not
    met, while \c True reports that the required native path is unavailable.

    The driver supports NULL, boolean, integer, finite floating-point, arbitrary-precision number,
    string, binary, and absolute date/time Qore values. Strings and binary data preserve NUL, tab,
    newline, carriage-return, backslash, and Control-Z bytes through MySQL's text-load escaping.
    Relative date/time values and container/object values are rejected by the native serializer.
    Identifiers are limited to MySQL's 64-byte per-component maximum.
    MySQL warnings, including conversion and duplicate-key warnings, fail the operation so that the
    internal savepoint can roll the entire native load back instead of silently accepting partial or
    truncated data.

    A savepoint spans all native blocks. Successful completion releases the savepoint but does not
    commit; the loaded rows participate in the caller's transaction and can still be rolled back with
    \c Datasource::rollback(). Aborting the operation rolls back only to the internal savepoint, so
    transaction work performed before the bulk load is preserved. Connection close and explicit
    transaction rollback abort an active native load, and commit is rejected while one is active.

    The driver owns mutation-observer stream events on the native path. Consumed bytes are the exact
    callback payload, including field separators, line terminators, and extra escape bytes. The
    ordinary fallback remains owned by BulkSqlUtil. The only supported native option is the common
    \c "stream_bounds" boolean passed by BulkSqlUtil.

    @note Connections built with native support enable the client protocol capability required by
    \c LOCAL \c INFILE, but install a permanent deny-by-default callback. Raw SQL cannot make the
    client read an arbitrary local path; only the internal in-memory source is exposed while a native
    bulk block is active.
*/
